# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored), fill in, and run `pnpm --filter @tempo/admin-web dev`.
# VITE_API_URL: the dev API URL (docs/claude-memory/project-status.md).
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN: https://tempo-<env>-<account id>.auth.eu-central-1.amazoncognito.com
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID: the tempo-<env>-admin-web app client, from
#   aws cognito-idp list-user-pool-clients --user-pool-id <tempo-<env>-users pool id> --profile tempo --region eu-central-1
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=
# VITE_COGNITO_MFA_SETUP: "true" lets the sign-in that two-step sign-in setup (/account/security) starts ask for the
#   aws.cognito.signin.user.admin scope; other sign-ins never ask for it. Turn it on only once the admin-web app
#   client allows that scope, or that sign-in fails.
VITE_COGNITO_MFA_SETUP=
